<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply falls in March.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply falls in March.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply fell by C$80 million to C$68.32 billion in March from C$68.40 billion in February, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   Mar 97     Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.32	68.40	59.02</p>
<p>M2					 391.84     392.54     389.03</p>
<p>M3					 506.02     500.27     475.88</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets		     March	February</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.69	-19.81</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     705.42	693.12</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    108.03	105.87</p>
<p>				    Wk to Apr 16  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.772  -0.143     +0.821</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     8.170  -0.427     -0.036</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	463.024  -0.637     +0.813</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 132.200  -0.600    -31.100</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.817  -0.034     +2.135</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
